          "filename": "Beach, Seafield. - geograph.org.uk - 49302.jpg",
          "caption": "Beach, Seafield. The maps suggest that this is only visitable, if at all at times of a very low tide.  On the ground however, there is more of the square exposed than expected. \nThe beach here will only be exposed at spring tides, and will be nearly two metres beneath the sea at neap tides. \n\nSeafield beach is Potobello's poor brother, languishing behind a car showroom strip mall.",
